# std/runner (design/caos-expr.md): the pooled interpreter every compiled worker
# is curried onto. Part of the irreducible SEEDED core — it is a self-contained
# nix closure with no source in this tree to build FROM, so like flake-builder it
# names a sentinel image and the core-seeder-runner answers with the pre-built
# delta. The sentinel is distinct (`docker://seeded-runner`) so its key cannot
# collide with another minimal-entry core item's.
#
# It exists as an ENTRY, rather than the raw delta it used to be published as,
# because a `DEPS` line has to name a PATH: `std/rustc/DEPS` says `../runner`,
# and a tree cannot be self-resolving if one of its dependencies is not in it.
# That is also what lets the repo-root `.caos-expr` deepen this tree at all.
run docker://seeded-runner -- --in:@=.
